It appears to be my turn to post about the next London rgrn meet.  For
the newbies in the audience, this is when a group of Nethackers meet
in a pub in London to eat, quaff and #chat about Nethack and related
topics.

Traditionally this occurs on the last Saturday of every other month,
so this month's meet would be Saturday 27 September.  However, that's
the day Ali gets back from his holiday, so he might not be able to
attend (I've just emailed him to ask).  Therefore it might be better
to postpone the meet until Saturday 4 October.  If you are planning to
attend, and have a preference for one or the other of those dates,
please post about it.

In any case, the meet will start at 14:00, and will be at the Lord
Moon of the Mall, Whitehall.  The directions (thanks to Dylan):

The LMotM is at the top of Whitehall; maybe a hundred yards down, on
the right-hand side as you go down from Trafalgar Square. Nearest tube
Charing Cross, though Westminster isn't that much further away for
those for whom that's quicker to get to. Look for people who are
either outright wearing NetHack T-shirts, or just looking generally
geek-like.

Eva.

